From: Kryxzort <101042137+Kryxzort@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 20:46:56 +0530
Subject: [PATCH 75/90] shader: TEX<n>FORMAT from each bound texture's format

WE defines TEX<n>FORMAT for every sampler slot 0..9 whose annotation has `formatcombo`, to the
format of the texture bound there or, with none, of the sampler's default (GH 0x1401d2a20:
"TEX" + n + "FORMAT" = the texture's format field). The stock common_fragment.h reads them
(DecompressNormal on TEX1FORMAT: DXT and RG88 normal maps unpack differently; fur4 reads
TEX8FORMAT). LWE set only TEX0FORMAT (RG88 / R8 of the layer's texture) and 0 for the rest.

Now a pass resolves what setupTextureUniforms will bind at the slot (a bind, the effect's
user / plain texture overrides, the pass's user / plain textures, the sampler's default), and
the formatcombo define takes its format: an FBO's, a .tex's (a JPEG / PNG .tex is RGBA8, 0).
A `previous` bind is an RGBA target (0). TEX0FORMAT stays as CPass sets it.

Origin: ours
Why: docs/player/spikes/we-lwe-gap-audit.md "Shader preprocessing result" (E20); we-coverage.md
Status: candidate-for-upstream
Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
